SUMMARY:Saturday Freethought Conversations
DESCRIPTION:Lancaster Freethought Society\n**July 18 Discussion: Free Inqu
 iry —**\n***What Does It Mean to Ask Without Fear?***\nFree inquiry is t
 he courage to ask real questions before we know the answer. It means we ca
 n examine ideas\, institutions\, traditions\, and assumptions without bein
 g punished for curiosity.\n\n**Ground rules**\nTimed rounds. Up to 2 minut
 es each. Option to pass. No interruptions. Open discussion after every 2 r
 ounds.\n\n**Q1 — Curiosity**\nWhat is a question you think people should
  be freer to ask?\n\n**Q2 — Fear**\nWhat makes certain questions feel ri
 sky: social pressure\, religion\, politics\, identity\, reputation\, or fe
 ar of conflict?\n\n**Q3 — Limits**\nAre there responsible limits to free
  inquiry? If so\, where?\n\n**Q4 — Community**\nWhat does a group need i
 n order to question honestly without becoming cruel\, reckless\, or perfor
 mative?\n\n**Closing Question** \\- What is one inquiry habit you want to 
 strengthen?\n(Choose one: courage\, curiosity\, patience\, precision\, goo
 d-faith listening\, asking better follow-up questions\, or tolerating disc
 omfort.)\n\nCome curious. Come ready to listen.
